<title>ITALY: Rome air cargo falls 12.7 pct in first quarter.</title>
<headline>Rome air cargo falls 12.7 pct in first quarter.</headline>
<text>
<p>ROME, April 24 (REUTER) - Cargo traffic handled through Rome airports fell by 12.7 percent in the first quarter of 1997, the airport authority said.</p>
<p>Air traffic details are shown below.</p>
<p> Mar 1997	Cargo	Pct change     Mail	    Pct</p>
<p>Change</p>
<p> Fiumicino     21,533     down 8.6	 3,670	   up 8.3</p>
<p> Ciampino	   803     up  23.9	     0	   n/a</p>
<p> Total	   22,336     down 7.8	 3,670	   up 8.3</p>
<p> Jan-Feb 97    Cargo	Pct change     Mail	    Pct</p>
<p>change</p>
<p> Fiumicino     55,717     down 13.8	10,723	  up 10.2</p>
<p> Ciampino	 2,347     up   25.7	     0	  n/a</p>
<p> Total	   58,064     down 12.7	10.723	  down 10.2</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
